Crucially, this does not excise regions of the space. The model still \emph{can} represent and potentially visit sequences that earlier training allowed. But the gradients now punish such moves. The effect is a thickening of wells around certain rhetorical styles and a steepening of slopes away from others.

The politics of RLHF live in its data. Who are the annotators? What instructions are they given? Which values are they told to reward? How is their labour organised and paid? Investigative reporting has documented annotators working under time pressure, with little context, applying policy guidelines that frame religious, sexual, and political content as varying degrees of risk.\footnote{See Billy Perrigo, ``Exclusive: OpenAI Used Kenyan Workers on Less Than \$2 Per Hour to Make ChatGPT Less Toxic,'' TIME, 18 January 2023, on Sama contractors in Kenya. For analogous accounts of crowdworker conditions, see reporting on platforms such as Remotasks and Scale AI.} Under such conditions, articulations that are dense, ambivalent, or culturally specific tend to be disfavoured; safe-seeming paraphrase wins.

